<article class="env-lemma" id="02JJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02JJ">Lemma <span data-tag="02JJ">10.36.5</span>.</a> Let $R \to S$ be a ring map. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$R \to S$ is finite, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$R \to S$ is integral and of finite type, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
there exist $x_1, \ldots , x_ n \in S$ which generate $S$ as an algebra over $R$ such that each $x_ i$ is integral over $R$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Clear from Lemma <a href="/tag/00GM" data-tag="00GM">10.36.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>